<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee areas seen safe from frost this week.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee areas seen safe from frost this week.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's key coffee regions are set to remain frost-free in the next few days as a low pressure system entering on May 27 increases cloud cover, preventing the formation of frost, independent meteorologist Somar said.</p>
<p>&quot;Temperatures are low in the coffee regions,&quot; said forecaster Marcos Massari. For instance, early morning temperatures in southern Minas Gerais were around 10 degrees Centigrade, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;But tomorrow a new low pressure system is entering, causing an increasing in cloudiness and rains,&quot; he said. &quot;This prevents the formation of frosts.&quot;</p>
<p>Traditionally, Brazil's coffee regions only come under real threat of frost from June to mid-August.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsrom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
